<title>SWITZERLAND: Safra Republic says Q1 up 30 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Safra Republic says Q1 up 30 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>January 1 to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>				    (million U.S. $ unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			57.2		vs 44.0</p>
<p> Interest income		240.6	     vs 244.2</p>
<p> Interest expense	     167.9	     vs 180.7</p>
<p> Net interest income	  72.7		vs 63.5</p>
<p> Credit loss provisions     7.0		 vs 3.0</p>
<p> Operating profit	     47.5		vs 31.0</p>
<p> Operating expenses	   48.4		vs 43.3</p>
<p> Net per common share ($)   3.24		vs 2.50</p>
<p> Shareholder equity	   1,705	     vs 1,490</p>
<p> Total assets		   17,997	    vs 15,676</p>
<p>Avg common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		   17,642	    vs 17,592</p>
<p>NOTE - Safra Republic Holdings S.A. is the holding company for six wholly-owned banks active in international private and commercial banking. They operate under the name of Republic National Bank of New York and are located in Switzerland, Luxembourg, Monaco, France, Guernsey and Gibralter. Republic New York Corporation hold 49.9 percent of the shares and Edmond J. Safra, through Saban S.A., holds 20.8 percent. The remainder are held by individual and institutional investors.</p>
<p>Safra said its shares were listed on the Swiss and Luxembourg stock exchanges and traded over the counter in London on SEAQ.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
